    "after": "Current root-proposed disposition, grounded in the original51/52 supplier-consumer owner full pre/post/current review (no new native review): The old full-space Borel claim lacked the zero extension from Q_r, and the old F6 attributed gradient closure/Pythagorean identification to a supplier that only provides the minimal-action theorem. Current step 1.1 explicitly extends by zero; step 2.3 proves gradient closure by Moreau envelopes, cutoffs and mollification. Step 3.1 subtracts continuity equations, obtains orthogonality against gradients and uses the proved closure to derive ||w||^2=||v||^2+||w-v||^2. Thus the stated velocity is minimal and the actual F6 identifies its action, without a stronger imported theorem or any scope restriction."
